    "text": " opened his desk drawer and began organizing his files. The attorneys would need every record, every communication, every trace of the machine he had built. He reached for a shredder bin and then stopped. Copies were already being downloaded around the world. For the first time in 40 years, destroying a document would change nothing. Somewhere in the cold Eastern European city, he looked out from the window and returned to his now excused apartment. The light of the apartment was dark, an economy more than a single stream of command. Centuries have been unfurled. May the last terrible lights of the apartment and the creaking doors driving away in the continuing traffic of every big city lights. Incognito, eyes fixed on the open sky, the bare fibers of lamp posts and relics of history, He could not see it. Brussels looked exactly the same. Cars, pedestrians, a woman arguing with a parking meter, a dog urinating on a lamppost with the serene confidence of a creature unburdened by ethical frameworks. But somewhere in the electromagnetic spectrum, in the fiber optic cables beneath the streets,",
